  "question": {
    "text": "Proton <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and electron <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>)</mo></math> will have same de-Broglie wavelength when the ratio of their momentum is (assume, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1849</mn></math>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></math>)"
  },
